.nh
.TH "GTREE" "1" "Sep 2026" "gtree dev" "gtree Manual"

.SH NAME
.PP
gtree-status - Scan a directory and display git repository status


.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBgtree status [path] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Scan a directory tree for git repositories and display their
status in a nested, styled tree view.

.PP
Examples:
  gtree status                 Scan current directory
  gtree status ~/Projects      Scan a specific path
  gtree status . --depth 3     Limit recursion depth


.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default ~/.config/gtree/config.yml)

.PP
\fB-d\fP, \fB--depth\fP=0
	maximum recursion depth (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable color output

.PP
\fB--only-dirty\fP[=false]
	hide clean repositories

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--sort\fP=""
	sort order: dirty|recent|name (default from config)

.PP
\fB--watch\fP[=false]
	live-refreshing view (polls every few seconds)


.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBgtree(1)\fP
